 a second pawn in the center, complementing the pawn on e4. This establishes strong control over the d5, e5, c5, and f5 squares, grants White a significant space advantage, and opens lines for the Queen and the dark-squared Bishop. This is the standard best response to passive play in the opening.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4'}
