uare. While Q: d1-h5+ delivers a check due to the empty f7 square, Black can easily block with ...g6, forcing the Queen to retreat and losing White time. Thus, solid development is superior to a premature attack.\n\nReason: N: b1-c3 develops a piece, solidifies the center by protecting e4, and prepares to meet Black's plan of ...Bb7. It maintains White's spatial advantage and flexibility.\n\nAnswer: N: b1-c3"}
