ck Rook on h8 and removes a key defender (the g7 pawn) from the Black King's shelter, exposing the King to further attacks.\n4.  **Tempo**: It forces Black to respond to the threat against their Rook or King, keeping the initiative.\n\nOther moves, such as moving the d5 pawn or moving the knight, ignore the threat to the Bishop or are less forceful. Since White is winning, preserving material while keeping the attack going is the best strategy.\n\nReason: The White Bishop at h6 is en prise (threatened by the pawn at g7). Capturing on g7 is the best way to save the piece, as it simultaneously wins material and creates a strong threat against the Black Rook and King.\n\nAnswer: B: h6-g7"}
